        "original_id": "c78132fa-17c3-575b-843c-fe28d0c86b3b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Forbidden Creatures; No Animals Were Harmed\n- People: Travis; Charla Nash; the author\n- Topics: Exotic animal ownership; illegal animal smuggling; animals in entertainment; animal abuse\n\nFacts:\n- In 2009, Travis attacked Charla Nash.\n- Forbidden Creatures focuses strongly on Travis, the chimpanzee who attacked Charla Nash in 2009.\n- Forbidden Creatures explores the lives of people who own exotic animals and people who were caught illegally smuggling them.\n- No Animals Were Harmed examines how people who work with animals define the boundary between using animals for entertainment and abusing them.\n- In No Animals Were Harmed, the author recounts that his own views about that boundary changed as he spoke with different people about their beliefs.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "0acf4a17-5d93-57b8-be48-0c136f807a64",
        "text": "Page: Forbidden Creatures. Sentence: The book explores the lives of those that either own exotic animals or have been captured for illegally smuggling them, with a strong focus on Travis, the chimpanzee who attacked Charla Nash in 2009.\nPage: No Animals Were Harmed (book). Sentence: The book explores what those who work with animals believe to be the line between using animals for entertainment purposes and abusing them.\nPage: No Animals Were Harmed (book). Sentence: Meanwhile, the author recounts how his own opinions changed about that line when he talks to the different people about their beliefs.",
